From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:48:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: sw43402: slice_count is slices per line, not per
 packet

The driver set slice_count = 1, correct for the tree it was written
against, whose dsi_update_dsc_timing() read the field as slice-per-packet
and derived the real slice count from hdisplay / slice_width itself.

msm now uses the field with its standard meaning: slice_per_intf,
total_bytes_per_intf, pkt_per_line and the MDP stream width all scale
with it. With 1 on this two-slice panel the DSI frames half a line per
packet: the left slice of every line decodes, the right slice
desynchronises into DSC noise. Set the real value, 1440/720 = 2.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c
index 34e0f1f4b6a5..2f6ce7ad1e21 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c
@@ -476,7 +476,14 @@ static int lg_sw43402_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 
 	dsc->slice_height = 16;
 	dsc->slice_width = 720;
-	dsc->slice_count = 1;
+	/*
+	 * Slices per line (1440/720), the field's standard meaning: msm sizes
+	 * the MDP stream from it (bytes per line, packets per line). The old
+	 * fork read it as slice-per-packet and recomputed slices itself, so 1
+	 * was correct there; here 1 halves the stream and only the left slice
+	 * of each line decodes.
+	 */
+	dsc->slice_count = 2;
 	dsc->bits_per_component = 8;
 	dsc->bits_per_pixel = 8 << 4; /* 1/16th units, 8.0 bpp; 6.18 msm rejects fractional */
 	dsc->block_pred_enable = true;
